{"id": "wd-Q19920734", "status": "ok", "meta": "Paul Revere gallops through a lit-up Lexington seen from above in Grant Wood's Midnight Ride of Paul Revere, 1931.", "about": "The Midnight Ride of Paul Revere is a painting of 1931 by Grant Wood. It shows Revere on his ride of 18 April 1775, seen from high above as he rides through a brightly lit Lexington, Massachusetts. It was inspired by Henry Wadsworth Longfellow's poem of 1860, and Wood used a child's hobby horse as the model for Revere's horse. The painting is in the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York.", "museum_record": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrant_Wood%2C_The_Midnight_Ride_of_Paul_Revere%2C_1931_(34571304085).jpg", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrant_Wood%2C_The_Midnight_Ride_of_Paul_Revere%2C_1931_(34571304085).jpg", "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q19920734", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Midnight_Ride_of_Paul_Revere_(painting)"], "check": "clean"}
