{"id": "si-chndm_1959-85-53", "status": "ok", "meta": "A bedroom alcove with a rocaille headboard and scalloped canopy, a panelling design by Nicolas Pineau, about 1720.", "about": "This design shows a bedroom niche with a bed. The headboard is high and in a rocaille pattern, with a scalloped canopy, and the upper part of the niche frame is richly carved in rocaille. The panel at the left has a rocaille design too, while the panel at the right is undecorated. Nicolas Pineau made it for his New Designs of Panelling, around 1720.", "museum_record": "https://collection.cooperhewitt.org/view/objects/asitem/id/124601", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://collection.cooperhewitt.org/view/objects/asitem/id/124601"], "check": "clean"}
