{"id": "wd-Q18214993", "status": "ok", "meta": "Joan of Arc imprisoned at Rouen in Pierre Révoil's Troubadour-style painting of 1819.", "about": "Joan of Arc Imprisoned in Rouen is a history painting of 1819 by Pierre Révoil, made in the Troubadour style fashionable in his day. It shows Joan of Arc in prison in Rouen during the Hundred Years War. Its composition was inspired by the neoclassical paintings of Jacques-Louis David. The final painting was shown at the Salon of 1819 in Paris, and a sketch for it is in the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York.", "museum_record": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AJeanne_d'arc_prisonni%C3%A8re_%C3%A0_Rouen-Pierre_R%C3%A9voil-MBA_Lyon_2014.jpeg", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AJeanne_d'arc_prisonni%C3%A8re_%C3%A0_Rouen-Pierre_R%C3%A9voil-MBA_Lyon_2014.jpeg", "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q18214993", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joan_of_Arc_Imprisoned_in_Rouen"], "check": "clean"}
